## Settings › Pen and handwriting (src/screens/settings/pen.rs).

settings-pen-finger = Draw with finger
settings-pen-finger-hint = Automatic: your finger draws until you use a pen on this device; after that it moves the page.
settings-pen-palm = Ignore palm
settings-pen-palm-hint = While the pen touches the screen, your hand neither draws nor moves the page.
settings-pen-double-tap = Pen double tap
settings-pen-double-tap-hint = On pens that support it (Apple Pencil 2, S Pen, pens with a button).
settings-pen-shortcuts = Shortcuts on the +
settings-pen-shortcuts-hint = Two bubbles above the + button to create something with one tap.
# $slot: 1 or 2.
settings-pen-shortcut-slot = Shortcut { $slot }
settings-pen-shortcut-none = None
settings-pen-shortcut-change = Change
settings-pen-shortcut-pick-hint = What the bubble creates with one tap.
settings-pen-writing = Writing
settings-pen-beautify = Beautify handwriting
settings-pen-beautify-hint = Each word straightens onto the line and evens out once you finish it. Your ink is kept: the lasso's Original brings it back.
settings-pen-snap-shapes = Snap shapes when holding
settings-pen-snap-shapes-hint = Hold the pen still at the end of a line, arrow, box or circle and it turns into a clean shape.
